<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Ticor says German Creek back to normal.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Ticor says German Creek back to normal.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ticor Ltd said on Tuesday that the Southern Colliery operations of the German Creek coking coal mine in Queensland's Bowen Basin had returned to normal after longwall mining was halted for 10 months.</p>
<p>The company, which has a 26.06 percent stake in German creek, said longwall mining had resumed in a different location and this would boost production by about 60,000 tonnes a week.</p>
<p>Shell Australia has a controlling 46.75 percent stake in German Creek. Ticor, a diversified mineral sands group, is about 35 percent owned by Iscor Ltd of South Africa. -- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
